From: PwndaWallet swap sidecar
Date: 2026-09-03
Subject: [PATCH 15/19] basicswap: Zano coin module (new files only)

Adds `basicswap/interface/zano/` -- the ZANO CoinInterface, its chainparams,
its prepare-module, and the JWT wallet-rpc transport. New files only; this
patch registers nothing, so it is inert until PWNDA-PATCH-16 wires ZANO into
`chainparams.py` / `basicswap.py` / `bin/prepare.py`.

Ported from REU26's proven 1,341-line `interface/zano.py`, re-pathed onto the
per-coin-folder layout this pin uses, preserving all 17 documented Zano
wallet-rpc quirks. Two deliberate Grove divergences from REU26, both
documented inline: (a) an `_external_main_wallet` flag (mirroring
PWNDA-PATCH-5's naming for XMR) makes `initialiseWallet` a logged no-op
instead of REU26's unconditional raise, because Grove's ZANO main wallet is
BY DESIGN the user's own host wallet and REU26's raise would fire on every
Grove startup; (b) `rpc.py` is a JWT client ported line-for-line from this
repo's own `src-tauri/src/zano_rpc.rs::build_jwt` (HS256, body_hash, single-use
salt, 60s exp, `Zano-Access-Token` header), which is live-verified against a
real Zano wallet-rpc.

`createWallet` is hard-gated to the SCRATCH connection only and raises if no
scratch connection is configured -- `generate_from_keys` is destructive and
one-way, and must never reach the host's main wallet.

RECONSTRUCTED 2026-09-03: this file was lost from `upstream/patches/` by an
orchestrating-session mistake (moved aside during an abandoned experiment,
then deleted with the scratch directory that held it). The patch BODY below
was regenerated by diffing two verified trees -- a freshly-built p14 tree and
