+                # serve the swap-engine-derived address, so REU26's raise would fire on
+                # every single Grove startup -- not a safety catch there, just permanent
+                # breakage. This logged no-op is the Grove-only substitute: it does
+                # nothing destructive and nothing that could provision the wrong wallet,
+                # and basicswap.py's getCachedMainWalletAddress (a SHARED file, not
+                # owned by this patch) then populates main_wallet_addr_zano from the
+                # LIVE wallet on first use, which is the correct swap destination in the
+                # host-wallet-sharing case.
+                #
